The '''Niamos Courthouse''' was a building on the planet [[Niamos]] which was used for the trials of those arrested by [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Coastal defender stormtrooper|forces]] on the planet. In [[5 BBY]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] was tried in this building following his arrest by imperial [[coastal defender stormtrooper]]s, and was sentenced by [[Unidentified judge|the judge]] to six years in the<ref name="Announcement" /> [[Narkina 5 Imperial Prison Complex]].<ref name="Narkina 5">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}}</ref>

==Description==
[[File:Niamos_courthouse_yard.png|thumb|left|280px|The Embarkation Yard with prisoners boarding the transports]]
The [[Niamos]] Courthouse<ref name="Insider 219">{{InsiderCite|219|Galactic Britain II: Cassian's Travels}}</ref> included a large hearing room where trials took place, including a tall desk for the presiding [[judge]] and one for a secretary equipped with an automated typewriter which he used to write sentencing cards with as well as a [[holopad]] screen. There was also a large [[Color|red]] banner behind the judge, bearing the [[Imperial crest]]. The room was staffed with [[coastal defender stormtrooper]]s carrying [[zap rod]]s during trials to keep the [[prisoner]]s in order and [[Lacertilo]] [[Unidentified bailiff|bailiffs]]. Behind the building was an<ref name="Announcement" /> Embarkation Yard<ref name="Insider 219" /> where at least three [[Imperial Troop Transport|Imperial prisoner transport ships]] could land and take off from. Prisoners were escorted to a staircase leading to the barge [[Hangar|landing pads]], from where they were directed to the barge headed to the prison they would serve their sentence in.<ref name="Narkina 5" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Niamos Courthouse first appeared in "[[Announcement]]," the seventh episode of the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' television series,<ref name="Announcement" /> which aired on [[October 19]], [[2022]].<ref name="Airdate">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-08-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref> 

The scenes of the courthouse were filmed at the [[Wikipedia:Carmel College, Oxfordshire|Carmel College]] in [[Wikipedia:Wallingford, Oxfordshire|Wallingford]], [[Wikipedia:Oxfordshire|Oxfordshire]], [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="Ep 7 Ep Guide">{{SW|url=series/andor/andor-episode-7-announcement|text="Announcement" Episode Guide &#124; Andor}}</ref><ref name="E8 Ep guide">{{SW|url=series/andor/andor-episode-8-narkina-5|text="Narkina 5" Episode Guide &#124; Andor}}</ref>

